[{:db/id "q-342279/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "e01f8219-8287-5e42-8b6f-0e6aef8da69d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342279/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ba9a2c64-19ca-57d5-8baf-357616ea7774" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342279/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "051705b9-ae61-5ff7-94eb-de5ff0fc39ff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342279/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "fc5251af-919c-5277-beb4-8315cb7f5822" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342279/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b9d7181a-b040-5211-823e-d5eb89465241" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342279/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7e7b23c-90f5-5f6a-943a-b792842b355a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-342279/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-342279/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-342279/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-342279/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-342279/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-342279/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342279" :question/id #uuid "84f40794-4c8b-5b6f-9373-bde070195026" :question/math-academy-id "q-342279" :question/problem "$$\n(x+1){y}^{″}+(x-3){y}^{′}+2xy=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a **singular** point of the differential equation above?\n\n- $x=-1$\n- $x=0$\n- $x=3$" :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both coefficients $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1){y}^{″}+(x-3){y}^{′}+2xy & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-3}{x+1}{y}^{′}+\\frac{2x}{x+1}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-3}{x+1}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{2x}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-1,$ since both denominators at $x=-1$ equal zero. So, $x=-1$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=0.$ So, $x=0$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=3.$ So, $x=3$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342279/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a9f9cf-06f6-51b8-ba41-a8b6300a5c2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c9fc30c5-8a2a-57fc-9e25-ba3be283de78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "7abe2d3d-c45a-5244-8841-72981651e3ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "1b3e72fc-aba8-50b4-a971-b6bbcd848924" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "2367f65d-004f-5796-b790-b734c9dca68f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "613fdb22-0ab7-5efb-ad6c-c90d61ce1acf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ef41485-5b71-5b7d-93e3-f8fa416ddd92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-342290/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-342290/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-342290/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-342290/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-342290/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-342290/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342290" :question/id #uuid "063c389f-2fc3-5dc6-9de5-5081febe5fa7" :question/math-academy-id "q-342290" :question/problem "$$\n(x-2)(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-1){y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is an **ordinary** point of the differential equation above?\n\n- $x=-3$\n- $x=0$\n- $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both coefficients $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x-2)(x+3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x+3){y}^{″}+(x-1){y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-1}{(x-2)(x+3)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x-2)(x+3)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-1}{(x-2)(x+3)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x-2)(x+3)}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-3,$ since both denominators at $x=-3$ equal zero. So, $x=-3$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=0.$ So, $x=0$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=2,$ since both denominators at $x=2$ equal zero. So, $x=2$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-342290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a9f9cf-06f6-51b8-ba41-a8b6300a5c2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342296/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "da1768b6-d22a-584e-9aa2-f374c940b8d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342296/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c7ffc1cc-4a2b-58d9-b88e-8a4cf4c25c28" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342296/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "73ad6a66-82d7-5d88-9cb2-6592d9fdea06" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensur