er.type/text :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342644/field-4/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" :answer/id #uuid "c07c711e-988f-5756-80dc-7b8a5960dc43" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342644/field-4/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937" :answer/id #uuid "a32343e9-9931-521e-b033-eff81e3fdced" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342644/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f144b050-a4b4-5469-b0f4-4253dbd22473" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342644/field-4/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" :answer-field/choices ["q-342644/field-4/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" "q-342644/field-4/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" "q-342644/field-4/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342644" :question/id #uuid "7d39c521-092e-5b02-9c9d-873965d15a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342644" :question/problem "$$\nx(x-9)(x+1){y}^{″}+(x-9){y}^{′}+x(x+1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y=0\n$$\n\nClassify the following points for the differential equation given above.$\\,$The point $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=-1$ is\n{{field-2}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=0$ is\n{{field-3}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=9$ is\n{{field-4}}\npoint of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nA singular point $x=a$ is regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $x(x-9)(x+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-9)(x+1){y}^{″}+(x-9){y}^{′}+x(x+1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{x(x+1)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-9}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{x(x+1)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-9}.\n$$\n\nThe function $P(x)$ is *not* analytic about points where $x(x+1)=0,$ which occurs at $x=0$ and $x=-1.$\n\nThe function $Q(x)$ is *not* analytic about points where $x-9=0$ or where $\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is undefined. These occur at $x=9$ and $x\\le 0.$\n\nTherefore, $x=3$ is $\\text{an ordinary}$ point of the differential equation, and the singular points are\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,x=0,\\,x=9.\n$$\n\nNow, let's classify each singular point.\n\n- For $x=-1,$ the function\n\n$$\n(x+1)P(x)=(x+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=-1,$ but the function\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}Q(x)=(x+1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-9},\n$$\n\nis undefined about $x=-1,$ so is *not* analytic about $x=-1.$ Thus, $x=-1$ is $\\text{an irregular singular}$ point of the differential equation.\n\n- For $x=0,$ the function\n\n$$\nxP(x)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x+1},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=0,$ but the function\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}Q(x)={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-9},\n$$\n\nis undefined about $x=0.$ So, $x=0$ is $\\text{an irregular singular}$ point of the differential equation.\n\n- For $x=9,$ the function\n\n$$\n(x-9)P(x)=(x-9)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x(x+1)},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=9,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x-9)^{2}Q(x)=(x-9)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-9}=(x-9)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nis also analytic about $x=9.$ Therefore, $x=9$ is $\\text{a regular singular}$ point of the differential equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-342644/field-1" "q-342644/field-2" "q-342644/field-3" "q-342644/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71f8b1c9-7856-52fa-8990-a83fda9ef2a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-342644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-342435/field-1/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" :answer/id #uuid "26f57c6b-8735-5304-b64f-7ac7d82013de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342435/field-1/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" :answer/id #uuid "63ffa458-2062-573b-8d33-19cbc14a72f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342435/field-1/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937" :answer/id #uuid "b3632dc9-1d5d-5138-9d02-e9d095027885" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342435/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb437e84-0a68-51a8-bf66-4a672ebbbd86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-342435/field-1/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" :answer-field/choices ["q-342435/field-1/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" "q-342435/field-1/1cdd626053dfdf43848942eac6640bb67468ab45f1203ea562ecf7407161f894" "q-342435/field-1/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-342435/field-2/711846b5f17da1e0f7b9c58c5ea67feac2751dddb68fa44a9c7038d9f8182937" :answer/id #uuid "d0503b38-1237-51b3-b240-92b1475c44c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-342435/field-2/dc7020e31a266715738fd921e33efbfc7b16ec3ae5c4b09a04e838c06763119c" :answer/id #uuid "08e64af8-1f39